{
  "_comment": [
    "Hoenn & Seek 2.0 (part 5): daily weather cycles. Read by tools/hoenn/gen_hoenn_weather.py,",
    "which writes src/data/hoenn_weather_cycles.h (the table src/hoenn_time.c uses).",
    "Every map below has one special-weather day in four: the day (weatherCycleStage + offset) % 4 == 2.",
    "The other three days it keeps the weather in its map header. Groups with different offsets storm on",
    "different days, so a region never all rains at once. On a map's special day its weather zones",
    "(coord-event weather, e.g. Route 120's patches) are ignored, so the special weather covers the map.",
    "weather: RAIN, RAIN_THUNDERSTORM, SNOW, FOG_HORIZONTAL or SANDSTORM (any WEATHER_* works).",
    "emerald: Routes 119 and 123 keep Emerald's own cycles (their zones translate the stage themselves);",
    "they're listed so events can ask about their special day (119's thunderstorm, 123's rain).",
    "Not listed on purpose: towns and cities, places that are always rainy or snowy (Olivine, Cianwood,",
    "Routes 17, 40, 41, 49, 50, Lake of Rage, Mt. Silver's snow, Sinjoh), forests (shade), Route 111's",
    "desert and Route 113's ash (their own zones), Safari Zones, and Alola."
  ],
